⚡🇰🇿🇷🇺Russian and Kazakh oil exports from Novorossiysk and Baltic ports fell 26% month-on-month to 6.1 million tonnes between August 1 and 21, per Vortexa and Kpler data cited by Argus and Kommersant. 

Shipments of Ural, Siberian Light, and Kazakh Kebco from Novorossiysk dropped 2.5-fold to 1.21 million tonnes due to vessel shortages. Charter costs are rising amid increasing military risks, causing shipowners to avoid sending tankers to the Black Sea.

